  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Lethedioside B may interact with SCCH-26 through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Lethedioside B is predicted to act as a target for Caspase-5, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-O-Methylcelebixanthone and cholesta-5,7,8(14),22E-tetraen-3-one. These compounds are all predicted to have a final score above 0.5, indicating a potential biological relevance. The shared targeting of Caspase-5 by different compounds suggests a possible mechanism of action, possibly involving the modulation of apoptosis or cell death pathways. The evidence supports a pathway where Lethedioside B may influence SCCH-26 through Caspase-5, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The consistency in the predicted targets across different paths strengthens the hypothesis, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
